   $q$The Latin root pend means "hang," and the prefix im- can mean "over" or "upon." What does "impending flood" mean in the last paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A flood that has been officially cancelled","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A flood that happened many years ago","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-frame"},{"text":"A flood that leaves sediment in the water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-word"},{"text":"A flood that is about to happen soon","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A flood that is about to happen soon$q$, $q$Something impending "hangs over" us, ready to arrive, and the county sends alerts "hours before the water reaches them." The pend root also appears in "suspended sediment," but that phrase describes particles in the water, not a coming flood.$q$, 'draft', '3a9ed744-5fee-5a76-b9b6-426a3d196390')
