   $q$The prefix con- means "with" or "together," and tempor means "time." Who were Josephine's "contemporaries"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"People who lived in the town at the same time she did","is_correct":true},{"text":"People who agreed with all of her ideas about books","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"People who study the town's history in modern times","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-time-reference"},{"text":"People who worked beside her inside the library","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$People who lived in the town at the same time she did$q$, $q$Contemporaries are people "together in time," and the passage says Josephine argued with them, including "her neighbors." Modern historians like Mr. Szabo live in the present, not in Josephine's time, so they are not her contemporaries.$q$, 'draft', 'edfad48f-1897-5b29-a6df-497e5fa046bb')
