   $q$The prefix im- can mean "in," and ped means "foot," so the word once suggested tangling someone's feet. What does "impede freight traffic" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Change the routes the trains take to the city","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Get in the way of the trains and slow them down","is_correct":true},{"text":"Help the trains move faster through the yard","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Count the number of trains that pass each day","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Get in the way of the trains and slow them down$q$, $q$To impede is to block or slow, like tangled feet, and the passage says such a delay "would cost the railroad money." Helping trains move faster is the opposite of a costly delay.$q$, 'draft', '561426fe-8037-5ada-8121-ba0a8b7ad0a4')
