   $q$The Latin root spir means "breathe." What does "His respiration had become short and ragged" describe?$q$, $q$[{"text":"His rowing stroke","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"His heartbeat","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-idea"},{"text":"His speaking voice","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"His breathing in and out","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His breathing in and out$q$, $q$Respiration contains spir, "breathe," and the sentence goes on to describe "each breath pulled in" and "pushed out." His stroke is mentioned in the same sentence, but the breaths are what became ragged.$q$, 'draft', 'a3d3f72a-582f-5852-b9e3-eadcd69bb2f6')
