   $q$The prefix per- means "through," and spir means "breathe," so the word suggests the skin breathing out moisture. What is the "Perspiration" that ran into Tomas's eyes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Spray from the river","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Rain from the clouds","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Sweat from his skin","is_correct":true},{"text":"Tears from his eyes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sweat from his skin$q$, $q$Perspiration is moisture that passes "through" the skin, which is sweat from a rower working hard. River spray is possible in a boat, but the word's parts point to the body, not the water.$q$, 'draft', 'a3d3f72a-582f-5852-b9e3-eadcd69bb2f6')
