  ('5aee3615-51e4-5126-a51c-760d36388e56', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix a- (from ad-) means "toward," and spir means "breathe," so the word suggests breathing toward a goal. What does "an aspiring rower" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A rower who has trouble breathing during races","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"A rower who would rather steer than pull an oar","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-characters"},{"text":"A rower hoping and working to become successful","is_correct":true},{"text":"A rower who has already won many championships","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A rower hoping and working to become successful$q$, $q$To aspire is to reach toward a goal, and Hana "had never raced in a final before," so she is still working toward success. Reading the word as a breathing problem takes the root too literally.$q$, 'draft', 'a3d3f72a-582f-5852-b9e3-eadcd69bb2f6')
