  ('598af202-2092-567f-bbd1-b52e5810550d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The suffix -ation turns the verb "inspire" into the noun "inspiration." What does Hana mean when she says, "That was my inspiration"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Watching the team gave her the motivation to race","is_correct":true},{"text":"Watching the team in the rain made her feel tired","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-context"},{"text":"Watching the team taught her how to breathe in","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Watching the team made her want to sit out","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Watching the team gave her the motivation to race$q$, $q$As a noun, inspiration names the thing that motivates someone, and Hana raced in the final after watching the team "practice in the rain all spring." She says she "nearly" sat out, so the inspiration is what kept her in the boat.$q$, 'draft', 'a3d3f72a-582f-5852-b9e3-eadcd69bb2f6')
