  ('3bd714c7-65a3-5c90-a266-833431be234c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The Latin prefix contra- means "against," and dict means "say." What does Wen mean when he says the bills "contradict what you were told"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bills repeat the same figure she heard on the phone","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"The bills prove that the spokesperson was correct","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The bills show something different from what she heard","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bills are too confusing for a student to read","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bills show something different from what she heard$q$, $q$Contra- plus dict means "say against," and the bills showed about twenty percent savings, not the half she was told. Saying the bills prove the spokesperson right ignores the "against" meaning of the prefix.$q$, 'draft', '5a67b95b-ebcb-5bb8-9b9d-986e52e1e701')
