  ('3c3e34fb-e4a3-5b32-bcd7-05f75993eab9', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The Latin root terr means "earth" or "land." What are the "terraces" described in the first paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Level steps of land cut into a hillside","is_correct":true},{"text":"Narrow channels that carry spring water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-term"},{"text":"Wide valleys found between two mountains","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Tall stone towers built on mountaintops","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Level steps of land cut into a hillside$q$, $q$Terraces are shaped earth, and the passage defines them as "a series of level steps that climb the slope." The channels carry water to the terraces, but they are a separate part of the system.$q$, 'draft', '1c3ac066-7dd6-5e4a-94b3-da82b7156735')
