  ('61bec77a-d319-5f65-8d60-264d22245922', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The Latin root aqua means "water," and duc (duct) means "lead." What are the "small aqueducts" the farmers built?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Wells drilled deep into the side of the mountain","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Walls that hold soil in place on each terrace","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-term"},{"text":"Ponds that store rainwater for the dry season","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Structures that lead water from one place to another","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Structures that lead water from one place to another$q$, $q$An aqueduct "leads water," and the passage says they carried water "from mountain springs to the highest terraces." A pond only stores water in one spot; it does not lead it anywhere.$q$, 'draft', '1c3ac066-7dd6-5e4a-94b3-da82b7156735')
