  ('7fc358e2-47a9-5b0d-9c2a-deefb05ddc90', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The prefix de- can mean "from," and duc means "lead," so to deduce is to lead a conclusion out from evidence. What do archaeologists do when they "deduce how many people once farmed an area"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They reason it out from clues like walls and channels","is_correct":true},{"text":"They read it in written records left by the farmers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-context"},{"text":"They guess a number without looking at any evidence","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They subtract the number of people who moved away","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They reason it out from clues like walls and channels$q$, $q$To deduce is to reach a conclusion from evidence, and the archaeologists do it "By examining the size of the walls and the layout of the channels." Subtracting is the meaning of deduct, a similar word that does not fit this sentence.$q$, 'draft', '1c3ac066-7dd6-5e4a-94b3-da82b7156735')
