   $q$The Greek prefix mono- means "one," and the root log means "word" or "speech." What is the "long monologue" in the second act?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A long scene change done in the dark","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-detail"},{"text":"A long pause with no words at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A long song sung by the whole cast","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"A long speech given by one actor","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A long speech given by one actor$q$, $q$Mono- plus log means "one speaking," and the passage says "the lead actor delivered" it alone. A song by the whole cast would involve many voices, not one.$q$, 'draft', 'cf302700-e714-5a6b-801b-1fb4a7876d9d')
