   $q$The root pend means "hang," and the suffix -able turns the verb "depend" into an adjective. What is "a dependable stage manager"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"One who has worked on many famous plays","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"One who relies on others to do the job","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationship"},{"text":"One who hangs the scenery above the stage","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"One whom others can rely on to do the job","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One whom others can rely on to do the job$q$, $q$Others "hang on" a dependable person, and Kofi is someone on whom "nearly everything rested." Reading it as someone who relies on others reverses who is doing the depending.$q$, 'draft', 'cf302700-e714-5a6b-801b-1fb4a7876d9d')
