   $q$The adjective "beneficial" comes from the same Latin source as the noun "benefit," with the adjective suffix -al added. What does the cast mean by "the most beneficial thing they could do for the shelter"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The action the shelter director had asked for","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The action that would help the shelter the most","is_correct":true},{"text":"The action that would make the cast most famous","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-context"},{"text":"The action that would cost the shelter the least","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-idea"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The action that would help the shelter the most$q$, $q$Beneficial means "producing good" or helpful, and a full house would bring in the most ticket money for the animals. Costing the shelter little is not the same as helping it; the word points to the good done, not to savings.$q$, 'draft', 'cf302700-e714-5a6b-801b-1fb4a7876d9d')
